flpanel -- the FreeLFS panel and start menu
===========================================

The bottom panel (44 px) and the start menu popup. One process, one fl_shell
binding (protocol: src/flcomp/protocol/fl-shell.xml). Needs flcomp; it exits
with a message under any other compositor.

Panel: start button, one entry per window, keyboard layout, Wi-Fi, volume,
battery (only when /sys has one), clock. Windows show their icon only;
panel_labels=1 in ~/.config/freelfs/desktop.conf adds the name (flsettings
has the switch). theme= and panel_labels= are re-read when the file changes.
Workspace pager (fl_shell 5, left of the layout indicator, only when there is more than one workspace):
a small grid, the workspace in view filled with the accent colour, cells with windows marked; a click
switches, the wheel steps, a right click shows the compositor's overview (Super+Tab).
Clicking a window entry activates it (going to its workspace), or minimizes it if it is focused. The
layout indicator cycles de, us, uk, fr (fl_shell set_keyboard_layout). Wi-Fi
opens flsettings; the battery opens its flyout (below), the clock the notification centre.

Menu: opened by the start button or by fl_shell's menu_toggle (Super).
Search, five categories, programs, Lock (greyed out until /usr/bin/fllock
exists; fllock asks flcomp for the lock, see src/fllock), Log out (fl_shell logout), Shut down (runs `poweroff`).
Programs are the .desktop files in the applications directory of $XDG_DATA_HOME
(default ~/.local/share) and every $XDG_DATA_DIRS entry (default
/usr/local/share:/usr/share); /usr/share, ~/.local/share/flatpak/exports/share
and /var/lib/flatpak/exports/share (what Flatpak exports) are always looked at.
Apps outside the four categories (games, media, graphics ...) show under All
programs. apps.py menu_dirs tests the search path. Beyond the usual keys, X-FreeLFS-Glyph=X sets
the character on the program's tile. Categories: Network/WebBrowser/Email ->
Internet; Office/TextEditor -> Office; System/Utility/TerminalEmulator/
FileManager/PackageManager -> System; Settings -> Settings.
Keys in the menu: type to search, Up/Down, Enter, Esc.
Entries whose program is not installed (TryExec, or the first word of Exec,
not found in PATH: GVim without its X11 build) are left out, as are NoDisplay
and Hidden ones. Terminal=true entries run in flterm; if the program fails the
window waits for Enter so the message can be read.

Tray (right side): battery from /sys/class/power_supply (not shown when there
is none; accent while charging, red at 15% or less), network from
/sys/class/net (Wi-Fi or wired icon, slashed when there is no link), volume
from wpctl. Volume: a click opens the flyout (flyout.c: slider, percent, mute button;
drag or click the bar, Left/Right/Up/Down 5%, PageUp/PageDown 10%, Home/End, M
mutes, Esc closes), scrolling over the icon changes it by 5%, a right click
mutes, and the laptop keys (XF86AudioRaiseVolume, LowerVolume, Mute, via
fl_shell volume_key) do the same. Every change shows at once and wpctl follows
in the background: only one wpctl runs at a time, and the latest wanted level
and mute state are what it is told, so a drag is a few calls. After the last
change one get-volume corrects the display if it differs. Changing the level
of a muted output unmutes it; opening the flyout never changes the volume. The
only timer besides the clock fires every 5 s, reads a few small files and
redraws only on a change; wpctl is asked in a child process through a pipe
(at start, after a change, every 25 s, once a minute while it keeps failing),
so the panel never waits for it.

Notifications (notify.c): the panel is the notification daemon, org.freedesktop.Notifications
on the session bus (spec 1.2: Notify, CloseNotification, GetCapabilities, GetServerInformation,
NotificationClosed, ActionInvoked; capabilities actions, body, icon-static, persistence), so
there is no second process. libdbus runs on a private connection whose fd is in flui's loop;
the panel starts before the session script starts dbus-daemon, so connecting is retried every
second (every ten after 90 tries). If another daemon owns the name the panel leaves it alone.
Desktop icons (deskicons.c, fl_shell 6 set_desktop): .desktop files with X-FreeLFS-Desktop-Icon=true
(and a TryExec that exists, so "FreeLFS install" only on the live system) get a flat tile with the glyph
and the name in a box at the top left of the screen, below the windows. Click selects, double click
starts. No such file, no surface.

Cards: a transparent surface at the top right of the screen (fl_shell 4 set_notifications), at
most four stacked, newest on top: tile (a built-in icon for known apps, else the first letter),
app name, summary, body (3 lines), up to three action buttons (the key "default" has no
button, it is the click on the card). Left edge: accent for normal, red for critical, grey for
low. They go away after 6 s (low 4 s; critical and expire_timeout 0 stay until dismissed; an
explicit timeout wins), wait while the pointer rests on the stack, and are dismissed by the
cross, a click on the card or an action. Not shown while the screen is locked (their time
starts when it is unlocked). Markup tags are stripped, the entities decoded; images
(image-data, image-path) and theme icons are not drawn.
Centre: click the clock. A flyout above it with Do not disturb (a switch; desktop.conf
notify_dnd=1; no cards for low and normal ones, critical ones still show, everything is in the
history), Clear all, and the history (50 entries, newest first, with a cross each, scrolls with
the wheel; a click on an entry runs its default action). A badge with the number of unread ones
sits left of the time, a slashed bell while Do not disturb is on. The history is kept in
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/flpanel-notifications (survives a panel restart, not the session).
Extra D-Bus interface org.freelfs.Notifications on the same object: SetDoNotDisturb(b),
GetDoNotDisturb, ClearAll, ToggleCenter, GetCount.
flnotify (libdbus only, like notify-send): flnotify [-a APP] [-i ICON] [-u low|normal|critical]
[-t MS] [-A KEY=LABEL]... [-r ID] [-T] [-w] SUMMARY [BODY] prints the id; -w waits and prints
"action KEY" / "closed REASON". flnotify --dnd on|off|toggle|status, --clear, --center, --count.

Battery (battery.c): the icon with the percentage is shown only when /sys/class/power_supply has a
BAT* (two batteries are added up; $FLPANEL_POWER_SUPPLY names another directory, tests);
accent while charging, red at 15 % or less, a small accent mark while power saving is on. Click:
a flyout with the level, state (on battery, charging, fully charged, plugged in not charging),
time left or until full (energy or charge over the smoothed rate, "Calculating" for the first
readings) and the draw in watts, and the Power saving switch. Power saving is desktop.conf
power_saver=1: flcomp dims the backlight to 70 % and draws at most 30 frames a second (src/flcomp
power.c), and the panel runs `flpower saver on` (setuid root, group seat), which sets every CPU's
governor to powersave and its energy preference to power, keeping the old values in
/run/flpower-saver for `flpower saver off`; at the start of a session with the setting on the CPU
part is applied again (the governor resets at boot). Warnings use the notifications: at 10 % a
card offers "Turn on power saving", at 5 % a critical one stays until the charger is plugged in;
each shows once per discharge (resets above 15 % or when charging starts).

Tests: make check (needs ../flcomp built, dbus-daemon, python3): tests/power.sh runs flpower against
a made-up cpu directory (FLPOWER_CPU and FLPOWER_STATE are honoured only when not root);
tests/notify.sh runs a private session bus, a headless flcomp, the real flpanel and flnotify
through ids, cards, stacking, expiry with reason, replace, CloseNotification, the click on a card,
Do not disturb, the centre (flnotify, clock click, Esc, click outside), history across a panel
restart, the lock, and low battery warnings (NOTIFY_OUT=DIR keeps screenshots).
FLUI_PPM=out.ppm flpanel --cards|--center|--battery renders made-up notification cards (out.ppm.3),
the centre (out.ppm.4) or the battery flyout (out.ppm.5) without a compositor.
FLUI_PPM=out.ppm flpanel --demo [--menu] [--volume] renders without a
compositor (out.ppm is the panel, out.ppm.1 the menu, out.ppm.2 the volume
flyout). FLPANEL_NOBAT=1 hides the battery. apps.py volume runs the tray with
a slow stand-in wpctl. FLPANEL_APPS=DIR replaces the
.desktop directories.

Build: make; make install (PREFIX, DESTDIR). Needs libflui.

Clock: calls tzset() each time it draws, so a new /etc/localtime (Settings > Date & time)
shows within the minute, at once when Settings sets tz_changed= in desktop.conf;
clock_24h=0 there switches it to 12-hour ("Mon 9 Nov  3:32 PM").
